{"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/VectorizationAndEmbeddings"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SwiftNLP"}],"title":"Text Normalization, Tokenization & Linguistic Tagging"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftnlp\/textnormalizationandtokenization"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/TextNormalizationAndTokenization"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clean text, strip punctuation, tokenize sentences\/words, tag parts of speech, extract entities, stem and lemmatize tokens, and score sentiment using NLTK-equivalent algorithms and Apple’s native "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NaturalLanguage"},{"type":"text","text":" framework."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Prepare raw unstructured text for machine learning pipelines with high performance and zero external dependencies.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"1. Multi-lingual Word & Sentence Tokenization","anchor":"1-Multi-lingual-Word--Sentence-Tokenization"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftNLP","","\/\/ Apple OS multi-lingual word boundary detection","let wordTokenizer = AppleWordTokenizer()","let words = wordTokenizer.tokenize(text: \"SwiftSci 2.5.0 is fantastic for NLP!\")","","\/\/ Sentence boundary tokenizer","let sentenceTokenizer = SentenceTokenizer()","let sentences = sentenceTokenizer.tokenize(text: \"First sentence. Second sentence!\")"]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"2. POS Tagging, Lemmatization & Entity Extraction","anchor":"2-POS-Tagging-Lemmatization--Entity-Extraction"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Part-of-speech tagging","let posTagger = POSTagger()","let tags = posTagger.tag(text: \"SwiftSci runs fast\")","\/\/ [TaggedToken(token: \"SwiftSci\", tag: .noun), TaggedToken(token: \"runs\", tag: .verb), ...]","","\/\/ Lemmatization (base canonical form)","let lemmaTagger = AppleLemmaTagger()","let lemmas = lemmaTagger.lemmatize(text: \"running faster\")","\/\/ [\"run\", \"fast\"]","","\/\/ Named Entity Recognition","let ner = AppleNamedEntityRecognizer()","let entities = ner.extractEntities(text: \"Tim Cook visited Apple in Cupertino.\")"]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"3. Sentiment Analysis (VADER & NLSentiment)","anchor":"3-Sentiment-Analysis-VADER--NLSentiment"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Pure Swift VADER Sentiment Analysis","let vader = VADERSentimentAnalyzer()","let score = vader.polarityScores(text: \"SwiftSci is an amazing library!\")","print(score.compound) \/\/ > 0.5 (positive)","","\/\/ Apple OS ML Sentiment Analyzer","let nlSentiment = NLSentimentAnalyzer()","let sentimentScore = nlSentiment.score(text: \"I love coding in Swift!\")"]}]}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://SwiftNLP/documentation/SwiftNLP/VectorizationAndEmbeddings":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/VectorizationAndEmbeddings","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftnlp\/vectorizationandembeddings","role":"article","title":"Text Feature Vectorization, Embeddings & Naive Bayes Classification","abstract":[{"text":"Convert text corpora into numerical feature matrices using ","type":"text"},{"code":"CountVectorizer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"HashingVectorizer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"TFIDFVectorizer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", query ","type":"text"},{"code":"WordEmbeddings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppleNLEmbedding","type